The initial C++ BPM formulas were translated through an earlier Python
translation of the Fortran expressions. That Python implementation and its
numerical baselines have been removed. Current numerical comparisons use
original Fortran only. The standalone C++ turbine implements the active
nine blade modes, aerodynamics, mesh transfers and acoustic driver of the
bundled case. It uses its own reduced Newton solve and Brent-Dekker root
implementation; it does not include the upstream mod_root1dim.f90 helper.
The empirical noise models are unchanged; this work does not introduce a
new noise model.

reference/fortran/dqk61.f contains SLATEC/QUADPACK's 61-point Gauss-Kronrod
routine for developer validation; its provenance comments are preserved.
The saved reference outputs were produced by original double-precision
Fortran runs. Python scripts only prepare inputs, run comparisons, export
plots, or manage toolchains. Intel oneMKL and the compilers are external
dependencies and are not redistributed in this repository.
